    {
      "text": "lights in the firmament … for signs, Gen. 1:14 (Moses 2:14; Abr. 4:14). they will believe the voice of the latter sign, Ex. 4:8. when that company died … they became a sign, Num. 26:10. shalt bind them for a sign upon thine hand, Deut. 6:8. giveth thee a sign or a wonder, Deut. 13:1. Lord himself shall give you a sign, Isa. 7:14 (2 Ne. 17:14). I and the children … are for signs, Isa. 8:18 (2 Ne. 18:18). Isaiah hath walked naked and barefoot … for a sign, Isa. 20:3. be not dismayed at the signs of heaven, Jer. 10:2. set thee for a sign unto the house of Israel, Ezek. 12:6. I am your sign, Ezek. 12:11. sabbaths … shall be a sign between me and you, Ezek. 20:20. he worketh signs and wonders in heaven, Dan. 6:27.",
